      "keyPath": "answerComponent.noDictionaryAvailable",
      "source": "No Dictionary Available",
      "translations": {
        "claude": "No hay diccionario disponible",
        "gpt": "No hay diccionario disponible",
        "gemma": "tags.\n\n    Translation: No hay diccionario disponible.\n\n    Wait, I'll check if \"No hay diccionario disponible\" is better than \"No se encuentra un diccionario disponible\".\n    \"No hay diccionario disponible\" is more direct.\n    \"No se encuentra un diccionario disponible\" is more \"formal\".\n    However, \"No hay diccionario disponible\" is not informal. It's neutral-formal.\n\n    Let's try \"No se dispone de diccionario\". This is very formal.\n    But \"No hay diccionario disponible\" is the most common and correct translation for this specific UI string.\n\n    Let's go with: No hay diccionario disponible.\n\n    Actually, looking at the source \"No Dictionary Available\", it's a status.\n    \"Diccionario no disponible\" is also a very strong candidate.\n    But \"No hay diccionario disponible\" feels more like a complete, polite message.\n\n    Let's refine:\n    \"No hay diccionario disponible\" (There is no dictionary available).\n    \"No se encuentra un diccionario disponible\" (A dictionary is not found available).\n\n    I will provide \"No hay diccionario disponible\".\n\n    Wait, I'll check if \"No hay diccionario disponible\" is too \"plain\".\n    If the user is \"all users\" and the tone is \"polite-formal\", \"No hay diccionario disponible\" is safe and professional.\n\n    One more thought: \"No se encuentra ningún diccionario disponible\". This is very formal.\n    But \"No hay diccionario disponible\" is the standard.\n\n    Let's look at the English again. \"No Dictionary Available\".\n    It's a bit clipped.\n    Spanish: \"No hay diccionario disponible\".\n\n    Final decision: No hay diccionario disponible.\n\n    Wait, I'll check if \"No se dispone de diccionario\" is better.\n    \"No se dispone de diccionario\" is very formal.\n    \"No hay diccionario disponible\" is standard.\n    Given \"polite-formal\", \"No hay diccionario disponible\" is appropriate.\n\n    Let's check if \"No hay diccionario disponible\" uses \"usted\". It doesn't use a pronoun, so it's neutral/formal.\n\n    Final check:\n    Source: No Dictionary Available\n    Target: No hay diccionario disponible\n\n    Wait, I'll consider \"No se encuentra un diccionario disponible\" one last time. It's a bit long for a UI component. \"No hay diccionario disponible\" is better.\n\n    Actually, \"No hay diccionario disponible\" is the most natural translation for \"No [Something] Available\".\n\n    One more check: \"No hay diccionario disponible\" vs \"No hay ningún diccionario disponible\".\n    \"No hay diccionario disponible\" is cleaner.\n\n    Final result: No hay diccionario disponible.No hay diccionario disponible\n\n<T>No hay diccionario disponible",
        "consensus": "No hay diccionario disponible"
      },
